{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1150500-guilty-pleasure","id":1150500,"title":"Guilty Pleasure","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-17T16:54:53-07:00","id":1150500,"title":"Guilty Pleasure","content":"I was thinking about the Guilty Pleasure Merit. I cannot decide whether it is a boon or a burden, if its rewards are worth its drawbacks (Hunger Management seems to provide similar benefits for much less hassle), and how to integrate it in the lifestyle of a Beast. I can certainly think of various indulgencies that would be appropriate for a mortal lifestyle, but the Merit is supposed to be used in the context of typical Satiety-hunting activities, and I can hardly think of how to integrate it with any of the Hungers. Could you kindly tell me your opinion about the Merit, and a few examples about how to mix its effects with the various Hungers ? Especially since every Beast is already supposed to have one specific preference in the context of their Hunger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 10-17-2017, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T17:23:01-07:00","id":1150505,"title":"","content":"Well think of it more as a specific aspect on the feeding as opposed to a thing you integrate into it. For example a normal tyrant feeding might be something like a need to dominate at contests, or games. For the guilty part maybe they get way more enjoyment than they think they should out of utterly destroying some kid who's on a winning streak in an arcade or something. They can also be a vulnerability. A ravager who likes to destroy people's sense of safety by breaking into &quot;secure&quot; areas and leaving notes or pictures taken of the person. Guilty pleasure, maybe they can't resist making at least one note handwritten, or every once in a while the pred makes it clear they shaved their legs using their victims razor. A nemesis might leave a calling card that could potentially be traced back if someone wanted to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T09:02:24-07:00","id":1150662,"title":"","content":"I see. So the Merit in practice has little to do with the typical human indulgencies for food, sex, drugs/booze, gaming, or whatever, and instead plays out as an even more special subtype with extra effects of the specific preference of feeding activities within one's Hunger that all Beasts have. The icing on the cake of the icing on the cake, so to speak. Good to know, and thanks for the claryfing advice. I'm still doubtful if the Merit is really worth to have, or Hunger Management effectively covers for most of its benefits with much less baggage. The benefits are good, but the Guilty Condition sure looks annoying to have (and RP) and rather troublesome to remove (unless say, confessing to your Brood or Family Ties companions is a valid resolution).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 10-18-2017, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T10:14:29-07:00","id":1150679,"title":"","content":"As opposed to needing to confess to what other individual? The restitution part I think would be trickier, but I think you would discuss that with the ST before you take the merit. Since you might need to discuss things like the individual you need to make restitution to, how hard it is to make it up to that individual, or even if you need to make restitution for it. Like can you leave five bucks on the bathroom counter with a note saying &quot;Used your razor to shave, get a new pack.&quot; How do you make it up to your family once you point out that you're targeting the immediate family of a victim from a few weeks back and you've still got a kid to hunt down and you'll go freaking nuts if you don't feed off that kid too; so of course you have to go even though the cops are probably watching the kid if they're involved at this point? If you're a collector going the phantom thief route and leave a calling card as a guilty pleasure do you need to make it up to anyone, or are you good with just being confronted with the newspaper article mentioning the theft by a broodmate and going, &quot;Oh you saw that. Yeah I left the card again, sorry.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T11:52:27-07:00","id":1150722,"title":"","content":"I see. Well, I wasn't even mindful of the restitution part and it makes the drawbacks even worse. You're right it takes some careful discussion with the ST before one would take the Merit. But your point makes me think in most cases the benefits of this Merit aren't worth the hassle, unless the character concept really calls for it - e.g. you are playing some kind of trademark addict such as Batman's Riddler. It seems much like the aforementioned Riddler, your restitution compulsion is going to buy you heaps of trouble by leaving up clues for Heroes, the cops, and your enemies to track. Otherwise, there are usually less troublesome ways of boosting one's Satiety supply.<br /> <br /> By the way, for the record, my preferred Hungers list more or less goes this way: Prey (very iconic, straightforward, easy to manage and to gauge in terms of desired nastiness) &gt; Punishment (much the same as the above with a narrower target list, playing the dark vigilante is a classic) &gt; Ruin (most features are similar to Prey/Punishment with a destroyer instead of an hunter archetype, but it requires enjoying waste for its own sake) &gt; Secrets (maybe; investigation may be fine, it depends on how much flexibility and leeway RAW and the ST shall give you with this) = Power (great if you like playing the social god with an established power base, but I often prefer playing the independent nomad) &gt; Transgression (being the corrupter once in a while may be fun, doing it all the time seems a real chore) &gt; Hoard (tiresome in all but the easiest cases, doubt I'm ever going to pick it for a PC).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 10-18-2017, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T16:42:23-07:00","id":1150825,"title":"","content":"Fair though I would point out that it would again depend on who restitution is owed to. While I could certainly see a nemesis feeling it necessary to make some form of apology if they feel their indulgence pushed the punishment over what the victim deserved; I also don't think it would be necessary for a nemesis to have need to apologize for say indulging in a particularly petty or embarrassing drive to punish people. Like if you had a nemesis who's guilty pleasure was they felt the need to punish people breaking rules at a strip club they might not want to cop to it to others due to then having to confess to frequenting strip clubs. Unless you went overboard you wouldn't need to apologize to the rule breaker, but you might have to apologize to others in your group for things like leaving them out of it, lying about where you were, or going to begin with depending on their stance.<br /> <br /> It doesn't require you to leave evidence. It just requires something that embarrasses your character, or something that causes a particular vulnerability. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> Beast core pg116</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It should be<br /> something that might embarrass her or put her in a vulnerable<br /> spot if revealed.</div> </div> </div> </div>So this doesn't necessarily mean the person needs to be aware of the thing you did. Just that if it became known you did so it would potentially cause you problems or humiliation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}